IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rta-types`
IMPORT `rta-dates`

-- Residential Tenancies Act 1986 — GOAL 3: TERMINATION.
--
--   "Is this notice to terminate lawful, and on what day may the tenant be
--    required to vacate; must the Tribunal terminate; and when do the
--    periods around termination end?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1986_120.txt — ss 50-66.

§ `Goal 3 — termination`

§§ `Termination by notice (ss 50, 51, 53, 53A, 55AA, 56A, 56B, 58A, 59-59B)`

-- s 50(1) "(a) in the case of a fixed-term tenancy, on the expiry of the term
-- of the tenancy or, if any of sections 55AA, 56A(1), 58(1)(d), (da), 58A,
-- 59, 59A, or 59B apply, by giving notice ...: (ab) by the sole tenant ...
-- giving notice of withdrawal under section 56B: (b) in the case of a
-- periodic tenancy to which a right of termination under any of sections 51
-- to 53A, 55AA, 56A(1), 58(1)(c), and 59 to 59B applies, by giving notice".
@ref s 50(1)(a)-(b)
GIVEN g IS A `Ground for notice`, k IS A `Kind of tenancy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground` g `is available for a` k `tenancy` IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `periodic` THEN NOT g EQUALS `s 58A a build-to-rent fixed term of at least 10 years`
    WHEN `fixed-term` THEN
            g EQUALS `s 55AA a physical assault for which a charge has been filed`
        OR  g EQUALS `s 56A(1) unlawful residential premises`
        OR  g EQUALS `s 56B withdrawal following family violence`
        OR  g EQUALS `s 58A a build-to-rent fixed term of at least 10 years`
        OR  g EQUALS `ss 59, 59A, 59B the premises are destroyed, uninhabitable or contaminated`

-- The minimum notice, in days, for the party giving it; NOTHING where the
-- section gives that party no right to terminate.
-- s 51 "(1) A landlord may terminate a periodic tenancy in any case by giving
-- at least 90 days' notice. (2) A landlord may terminate a periodic tenancy
-- by giving at least 42 days' notice if— (a) the owner ... requires the
-- premises ... as the principal place of residence ...; or (b) ... an
-- unconditional agreement for the sale ... vacant possession; or (c) ...
-- employees ... or contractors ...; or (d) ... a school board ... and the
-- landlord is the Crown. (2A) A tenant may terminate a periodic tenancy in
-- any case by giving at least 21 days' notice."
-- s 53 "(1) The landlord or the tenant may terminate a service tenancy by
-- giving at least 14 days' notice ... (4) Where the tenant of a service
-- tenancy dies leaving any dependant ..., the landlord may terminate ... by
-- giving at least 14 days' notice. (5) However, ... at least 5 days' notice
-- if ... a replacement employee [is needed] within less than 14 days".
-- s 53A(2) landlord or tenant, 14 days. s 55AA(1) landlord, 14 days. s 56A(1)
-- tenant, "not less than 2 days". s 56B(1) tenant, "at least 2 days". s 58A(2)
-- tenant, 56 days. ss 59(2)-(3), 59A(4)-(5), 59B(6)-(7) landlord 7 days,
-- tenant 2 days.
@ref ss 51(1)-(2A), 53(1), (4)-(5), 53A(2), 55AA(1), 56A(1), 56B(1), 58A(2), 59(2)-(3), 59A(4)-(5), 59B(6)-(7)
GIVEN g IS A `Ground for notice`, who IS A `Who gives notice`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the minimum notice in days on the ground` g `, given by` who MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `s 51(1) the landlord, in any case` THEN landlord 90
    WHEN `s 51(2)(a) the owner or family will live there` THEN landlord 42
    WHEN `s 51(2)(b) an unconditional sale needs vacant possession` THEN landlord 42
    WHEN `s 51(2)(c) required for employees or contractors, as stated in the agreement` THEN landlord 42
    WHEN `s 51(2)(d) required for school board employees or contractors (the Crown), as stated in the agreement` THEN landlord 42
    WHEN `s 51(2A) the tenant, in any case` THEN tenant 21
    WHEN `s 53(1) the service contract has ended or notice of its end was given` THEN JUST 14
    WHEN `s 53(4) the service tenant died leaving a dependant` THEN landlord 14
    WHEN `s 53(5) the service tenant died and a replacement is urgently needed` THEN landlord 5
    WHEN `s 53A(2) the tenant is no longer eligible for the student tenancy` THEN JUST 14
    WHEN `s 55AA a physical assault for which a charge has been filed` THEN landlord 14
    WHEN `s 56A(1) unlawful residential premises` THEN tenant 2
    WHEN `s 56B withdrawal following family violence` THEN tenant 2
    WHEN `s 58A a build-to-rent fixed term of at least 10 years` THEN tenant 56
    WHEN `ss 59, 59A, 59B the premises are destroyed, uninhabitable or contaminated` THEN
        IF who EQUALS `the landlord` THEN JUST 7 ELSE JUST 2
    WHERE
        GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
        landlord n MEANS IF who EQUALS `the landlord` THEN JUST n ELSE NOTHING
        GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
        tenant n MEANS IF who EQUALS `the tenant` THEN JUST n ELSE NOTHING

-- s 136A: the period of notice "(a) commences on the first day after the
-- notice is given or deemed to be given under section 136; and (b) ends with
-- the close of the last day of the period." s 51(5): the notice "may be
-- given on any day, and the period of notice may be expressed to expire on
-- any day". s 53(3) "No notice under this section shall have effect to
-- terminate a service tenancy on a date preceding the date on which the
-- termination of the contract of service ... takes effect."
@ref ss 51(5), 53(3), 56C, 136, 136A
@export The earliest day a notice to terminate may require the tenant to vacate under the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): the last day of the minimum notice period (90 days, 42 days with a s 51(2) ground, 21 days from a tenant, 14, 5, 7, 56 or 2 days under the other sections), counted from the day after the notice is given or deemed given under s 136 (4 working days after posting, 2 after delivery to a mailbox), and for a service tenancy not before the service contract ends. Nothing if the ground is not available to that party for that kind of tenancy. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Termination notice`  @desc Who gives the notice, the kind of tenancy, the ground, the day it was sent and how it was served, the date to vacate, whether it is in the required form, and when any service contract ends
      cal IS A `Local calendar`  @desc The Matariki Observance Days and local anniversary days
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the earliest date to vacate under the notice` n `, calendar` cal MEANS
    IF   NOT `the ground` (n's `ground`) `is available for a` (n's `kind of tenancy`) `tenancy`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the minimum notice in days on the ground` (n's `ground`) `, given by` (n's `given by`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST minimum THEN
             JUST (CONSIDER n's `service contract ends on`
                   WHEN JUST ends THEN later ends (periodEnd minimum)
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN periodEnd minimum)
    WHERE
        -- s 56C "(1) Despite section 136(6),— (a) if a notice of withdrawal
        -- under section 56B(1) ... [is] sent by post ..., [it is] to be treated
        -- as given to the landlord on the date on which [it is] posted ... (2)
        -- Despite section 136(7),— (a) ... delivered ... on the date on which
        -- [it is] delivered" (added after the independent pass).
        given MEANS
            IF       n's `ground` EQUALS `s 56B withdrawal following family violence`
                 AND (   n's `served` EQUALS `by post`
                      OR n's `served` EQUALS `by delivery to a mailbox or door`)
            THEN n's `notice of termination sent on`
            ELSE `the day a notice is deemed given, sent` (n's `notice of termination sent on`) `, served` (n's `served`) `, calendar` cal
        GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A DATE
        periodEnd k MEANS `the last day of a period of` k `days after notice given on` given
        GIVEN x IS A DATE, y IS A DATE
        GIVETH A DATE
        later x y MEANS IF x GREATER THAN y THEN x ELSE y

-- s 51(3) "Every notice to terminate a tenancy shall— (a) be in writing; and
-- (b) identify the premises ...; and (c) specify the date by which the tenant
-- is to vacate ...; and (ca) if the landlord gives less than 90 days' notice,
-- set out the reasons for the termination; and (d) be signed". (4) saves a
-- notice that does not mislead.
@ref ss 50, 51(3)-(4), 136, 136A
@export Whether a notice to terminate a residential tenancy is lawful under the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): the ground is available to the party for that kind of tenancy (s 50), the notice is in the required form (s 51(3)-(4), or the approved form), and the date to vacate is no earlier than the end of the minimum notice period counted under ss 136 and 136A. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Termination notice`  @desc Who gives the notice, the kind of tenancy, the ground, the day it was sent and how it was served, the date to vacate, whether it is in the required form, and when any service contract ends
      cal IS A `Local calendar`  @desc The Matariki Observance Days and local anniversary days
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the termination notice is lawful` n cal IF
        n's `in the required form`
    AND CONSIDER `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` n `, calendar` cal
        WHEN JUST earliest THEN n's `date to vacate` AT LEAST earliest
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

§§ `Termination by the Tribunal (ss 55, 55A, 56)`

-- s 55(1)(aa)(i) "an amount of rent has been owing for at least 5 working
-- days after the date on which it was due": still unpaid at the end of the
-- 5th working day after the due date.
@ref s 55(1)(aa)(i)
GIVEN o IS AN Occasion, cal IS A `Local calendar`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `rent was owing for at least 5 working days on` o cal IF
    CONSIDER o's `rent paid on, if paid`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST paid THEN paid GREATER THAN `the` 5 `th working day after` (o's `occasion on`) `, calendar` cal

-- "on 3 separate occasions within a 90-day period ... and ... the landlord's
-- application to the Tribunal was made within 28 days after the landlord gave
-- the third notice" (ss 55(1)(aa), 55A(2)). Occasions are listed in date
-- order. A 90-day period holds the first and third occasions if they are no
-- more than 89 days apart (fork F4).
@ref ss 55(1)(aa), 55A(2)
GIVEN os IS A LIST OF Occasion
      filed IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`3 occasions within 90 days, filed within 28 days of the third notice, list` os `, filed` filed MEANS
    CONSIDER os
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN a FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            (CONSIDER rest
             WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
             WHEN b FOLLOWED BY rest2 THEN
                 CONSIDER rest2
                 WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
                 WHEN c FOLLOWED BY more THEN
                         Day (c's `occasion on`) MINUS Day (a's `occasion on`) AT MOST 89
                     AND filed AT MOST `the day` 28 `days after` (c's `occasion notice given on`))
        OR  `3 occasions within 90 days, filed within 28 days of the third notice, list` rest `, filed` filed

-- s 55 "(1) ... the Tribunal shall make an order terminating the tenancy if
-- ... satisfied that— (a) the rent was, at the date on which the application
-- was filed ..., at least 21 days in arrear; or (aa) the tenancy is a
-- periodic tenancy and— (i) on 3 separate occasions within a 90-day period
-- an amount of rent has been owing for at least 5 working days ...; and (ii)
-- [a written notice each time] ...; and (iii) [each stating how many others]
-- ...; and (iv) the landlord's application ... was made within 28 days after
-- the landlord gave the third notice; or (b) ... substantial damage ...; or
-- (c) ... assaulted, or has threatened to assault [a listed person]. ... (3)
-- The Tribunal may refuse to make an order ... if, but only if, it is
-- satisfied that the breach has been remedied ..., the landlord has been
-- compensated ..., and it is unlikely that the tenant will commit any
-- further breach".
@ref s 55(1), (3)
@export Whether the Tenancy Tribunal must terminate a tenancy on the landlord's application under s 55 of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): rent at least 21 days in arrear when the application is filed; or, for a periodic tenancy, rent owing for 5 working days on 3 occasions within 90 days, each notified, with the application within 28 days of the third notice; or substantial damage; or an assault or threat — unless the breach is remedied, the landlord compensated and no further breach likely. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN a IS A `Termination application`  @desc The filing date, whether the tenancy is periodic, the days of arrears, the occasions of overdue rent (in date order) with their notices, damage and assault, and whether the breach is remedied
      cal IS A `Local calendar`  @desc The Matariki Observance Days and local anniversary days
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Tribunal must terminate under s 55` a cal IF
        (   a's `days of rent in arrear at filing` AT LEAST 21
         OR (    a's `periodic tenancy`
             AND a's `each occasion notice had the required content`
             AND `3 occasions within 90 days, filed within 28 days of the third notice, list` owing `, filed` (a's `application filed on`))
         OR a's `substantial damage caused or threatened`
         OR a's `assault or threat against a person in s 55(1)(c)`)
    AND NOT a's `breach remedied, landlord compensated, no further breach likely`
    WHERE
        owing MEANS filter (GIVEN o YIELD `rent was owing for at least 5 working days on` o cal) (a's `rent overdue occasions`)

-- s 55A "(1) A landlord under a periodic tenancy may apply ... on the ground
-- of anti-social behaviour. (2) The Tribunal must (subject to subsection (3))
-- make the order if satisfied that— (a) on 3 separate occasions within a
-- 90-day period the tenant ... engaged in anti-social behaviour ...; and (b)
-- on each occasion the landlord gave the tenant written notice ...; and (c)
-- the landlord's application ... was made within 28 days after the landlord
-- gave the third notice. (3) However, the Tribunal must not make the order if
-- satisfied that— (a) doing so would be unfair ...; or (b) ... motivated ...
-- by the exercise ... by the tenant of any right".
@ref s 55A(1)-(3)
GIVEN a IS A `Termination application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Tribunal must terminate for anti-social behaviour` a IF
        a's `periodic tenancy`
    AND a's `each occasion notice had the required content`
    AND `3 occasions within 90 days, filed within 28 days of the third notice, list` (a's `anti-social behaviour occasions`) `, filed` (a's `application filed on`)
    AND NOT a's `s 55A(3) unfairness or retaliation shown`

-- s 56(1)(b)(i) "a notice ... requiring the other party to remedy the breach
-- within a reasonable period, being not less than 14 days commencing with the
-- day on which the notice was given". The period includes the day of giving,
-- so 14 days end on the 13th day after it.
@ref s 56(1)(b)
GIVEN given IS A DATE, allowed IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to remedy under a s 56 notice given on` given `, allowing` allowed `days` MEANS
    IF   allowed LESS THAN 14
    THEN `s 56 requires a remedy period of at least 14 days`
    ELSE `the day` (allowed MINUS 1) `days after` given

`s 56 requires a remedy period of at least 14 days` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 56(1)(b)(i): the remedy period must be at least 14 days"

§§ `Periods around termination (ss 50A, 56D, 60, 60A, 60B, 61, 62A, 62D, 64)`

-- s 50A(1) "the tenancy agreement terminates on the earliest of the following
-- dates: (a) the date that is the 21st day after the date on which the
-- personal representative ... or ... next of kin gives the landlord written
-- notice of the death ...: (b) the date that is the 21st day after the
-- landlord gives [them] ... written notice to vacate ...: (c) the date that is
-- agreed in writing ...: (d) the date determined ... by the Tribunal".
@ref s 50A(1)
GIVEN deathNotice IS A MAYBE DATE, vacateNotice IS A MAYBE DATE, agreed IS A MAYBE DATE, tribunal IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the tenancy ends after the sole tenant's death, notice of death` deathNotice `, notice to vacate` vacateNotice `, agreed` agreed `, Tribunal` tribunal MEANS
    earliest (plus21 deathNotice) (earliest (plus21 vacateNotice) (earliest agreed tribunal))
    WHERE
        GIVEN m IS A MAYBE DATE
        GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
        plus21 m MEANS
            CONSIDER m
            WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (`the day` 21 `days after` d)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        GIVEN x IS A MAYBE DATE, y IS A MAYBE DATE
        GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
        earliest x y MEANS
            CONSIDER x
            WHEN NOTHING THEN y
            WHEN JUST a THEN
                CONSIDER y
                WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST a
                WHEN JUST b THEN IF a AT MOST b THEN JUST a ELSE JUST b

-- s 56D(3) "Any application under this section must be made before the end
-- of the period of 60 days beginning with the day after the date of the
-- withdrawal."
@ref s 56D(3)
GIVEN withdrawn IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for a s 56D hardship application, withdrawal on` withdrawn MEANS
    `the day` 60 `days after` withdrawn

-- s 60(2) "If the landlord permits the tenant to remain ... for more than 90
-- days after the tenancy has terminated ..., without obtaining a possession
-- order, or for more than 90 days after obtaining a possession order, the
-- landlord shall be deemed to have granted ..., as from the date on which
-- that period of 90 days expired, a periodic tenancy".
@ref s 60(2)
GIVEN ended IS A DATE, order IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day a periodic tenancy is deemed granted, tenancy ended` ended `, possession order` order MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN JUST o THEN `the day` 90 `days after` o
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day` 90 `days after` ended

-- s 60A "(1) On the expiry of a fixed-term tenancy of more than 90 days, the
-- tenancy continues as a periodic tenancy ... (2) However, ... not ... if,—
-- (a) before the expiry, the parties renew or extend ...; or (b) before the
-- expiry, the parties agree not to continue ...; or (c) within the effective
-- period, either party gives to the other party written notice of their
-- intention not to continue ...; or (d) before the expiry, a party gives
-- notice as specified in any of section 50(1)(a) to (ac) that terminates the
-- tenancy on or before the expiry. (3) The effective period is the period
-- that starts on the 90th day before the date on which the tenancy expires and
-- ends on the 21st day before that date."
@ref s 60A
@export Whether a fixed-term tenancy continues as a periodic tenancy on expiry under s 60A of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): yes for a term of more than 90 days, unless the parties renewed or extended it or agreed not to continue, a party gave written notice not to continue between the 90th and the 21st day before expiry, or it was ended on or before expiry by notice. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A `Fixed term ending`  @desc The expiry date and length of the term, any renewal, extension or agreement not to continue, the day any notice not to continue was given, and any terminating notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenancy continues as a periodic tenancy` f IF
        f's `fixed term length, in days` GREATER THAN 90
    AND NOT f's `renewed or extended before expiry`
    AND NOT f's `agreed before expiry not to continue`
    AND NOT f's `ended on or before expiry by a notice under s 50(1)(a)-(ac)`
    AND NOT (CONSIDER f's `notice of intention not to continue given on`
             WHEN JUST g THEN g AT LEAST `the day` (0 MINUS 90) `days after` expiry AND g AT MOST `the day` (0 MINUS 21) `days after` expiry
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
    WHERE
        expiry MEANS f's `fixed term expires on`

-- s 60B(2) "The tenant must give notice of the tenant's intention not later
-- than the 21st day before the date on which the tenancy would otherwise
-- expire."
@ref s 60B(2)
GIVEN expiry IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to give notice to renew or extend, expiry` expiry MEANS
    `the day` (0 MINUS 21) `days after` expiry

-- s 61(3) "A tenant who abandons the premises shall ... be liable to pay the
-- rent for any period up to and including, but not after, the following date:
-- (a) in the case of a periodic tenancy,— (i) the date of the expiry of the
-- period of 21 days after the date specified by the Tribunal under subsection
-- (2); or (ii) the date of commencement of a new tenancy ...,— whichever is
-- the earlier: (b) in the case of a fixed-term tenancy,— (i) the date of the
-- expiry of the term; or (ii) the date of commencement of a new tenancy ...,—
-- whichever is the earlier."
@ref s 61(3)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of tenancy`, aware IS A DATE, expiry IS A DATE, next IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of rent after abandonment, tenancy` k `, landlord aware on` aware `, term expires` expiry `, new tenancy starts` next MEANS
    CONSIDER next
    WHEN JUST n THEN IF n LESS THAN base THEN n ELSE base
    WHEN NOTHING THEN base
    WHERE
        base MEANS
            CONSIDER k
            WHEN `periodic` THEN `the day` 21 `days after` aware
            WHEN `fixed-term` THEN expiry

-- s 62A(3) the landlord "must secure those goods in safe storage for not less
-- than 35 days from the date on which the landlord first took possession of
-- those goods"; (5) after that period the landlord may sell them. Clear days
-- from possession: the 36th day is the first on which they may be sold
-- (fork F5).
@ref s 62A(3), (5)
GIVEN possession IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day stored goods may be sold, possession taken` possession MEANS
    `the day` 36 `days after` possession

-- s 62D "At any time within 1 year after the date of a sale ..., the tenant
-- may apply to the chief executive for the payment ... of the proceeds".
@ref s 62D
GIVEN sold IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to claim the proceeds of sale, sold` sold MEANS
    `add years` sold 1

-- s 64 "(2) No possession order may be made more than 90 days after the date
-- of the termination of the tenancy. ... (4) No possession order ... shall be
-- capable of being filed under section 106 more than 90 days after— (a) the
-- date of the order".
@ref s 64(2), (4)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for a possession order or its filing, from` d MEANS
    `the day` 90 `days after` d
